---
import AdminNav from '../../components/AdminNav.astro';
import DfsSpend from '../../components/DfsSpend.astro';
import '@fontsource/sora/400.css';
import '@fontsource/sora/600.css';
import '../../styles/analytics-reports.css';
import '../../styles/seo-report.css';
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow"/><title>SEO & Analytics Reports | NC Digital</title></head><body>
<AdminNav />
<DfsSpend />
<header><a class="brand" href="/admin/links/">SEO &amp; Analytics Reports</a></header>
<main><div class="intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">CLIENT REPORTING · GA4 + SEARCH CONSOLE</p><h1>Show the progress.<br/><span>Explain the numbers.</span></h1><p>A clear view of search visibility, website visits and meaningful actions, with the previous period beside every figure.</p></div><div class="connection"><p id="connection">Checking Google access…</p><button id="refresh-connection" type="button">Refresh connection</button></div></div>
<section class="panel clients-panel" id="clients-panel"><p class="eyebrow">SAVED CLIENTS</p><div class="clients-row"><label>Client<select id="client-select"><option value="">Choose a saved client…</option></select></label><button id="client-run" class="primary" type="button" disabled>Create last month’s report ↗</button><button id="client-edit" type="button" disabled>Edit client</button><button id="client-new" type="button">New client</button></div><p id="client-summary" class="muted"></p>
<form id="client-form" class="client-form" hidden><h3 id="client-form-title">New client</h3><div class="client-grid"><label>Business name<input id="c-name" required maxlength="120" placeholder="e.g. IR Energy"/></label><label>Google Analytics property<select id="c-property" required></select></label><label>Search Console property<select id="c-site"></select></label><label>Country<select id="c-country"><option value="all">All countries</option><option value="gbr">United Kingdom</option></select></label><label>Town for ranking checks<input id="c-town" list="c-towns" maxlength="150" placeholder="e.g. Cardiff" autocomplete="off"/><datalist id="c-towns"></datalist></label><label>Contact name<input id="c-contact-name" maxlength="120" placeholder="Optional"/></label><label>Contact email<input id="c-contact-email" type="email" maxlength="254" placeholder="Optional, used to email reports"/></label></div>
<div class="client-grid wide"><label>Searches to track <span class="hint">one per line, up to 15 · about 0.6p each per report</span><textarea id="c-keywords" rows="5" placeholder="solar panels cardiff&#10;battery storage cardiff"></textarea></label><label>Other names people search for the business by <span class="hint">one per line · e.g. old names or short forms</span><textarea id="c-brand" rows="5" placeholder="ir solar"></textarea></label><label>Analytics events that count as enquiries <span class="hint">one per line · leave blank to detect automatically</span><textarea id="c-events" rows="5" placeholder="phone_click&#10;form_submit"></textarea><small id="c-events-hint"></small></label></div>
<div class="client-actions"><button class="primary" type="submit">Save client</button><button id="client-cancel" type="button">Cancel</button><button id="client-delete" type="button" hidden>Delete client</button><span id="client-status" class="muted" role="status"></span></div></form></section>
<section class="panel setup"><form id="form"><fieldset id="fields"><div class="form-grid"><label>Google Analytics property<select id="property" required><option value="">Loading properties…</option></select></label><label>Matching Search Console property<select id="site"><option value="">Analytics only</option></select><small>Select the same client’s website to include SEO figures.</small></label><label>Reporting period<select id="period"><option value="1">Last completed month</option><option value="3">Last 3 completed months</option><option value="6">Last 6 completed months</option><option value="custom">Custom dates</option></select></label><label>Country<select id="country"><option value="all">All countries</option><option value="gbr">United Kingdom</option></select></label></div><div id="custom-dates" class="date-fields" hidden><label>Start date<input id="start-date" type="date"/></label><label>End date<input id="end-date" type="date"/></label><p>Up to 184 days. Compared with the same number of days immediately before this range.</p></div><div class="form-footer"><p>Calendar periods compare with the preceding 1, 3 or 6 months. Web traffic only. No DataForSEO credits.</p><label class="checkbox"><input id="fresh" type="checkbox"/> Refresh saved data</label><button id="start" class="primary" disabled>Create client report ↗</button></div></fieldset></form></section>
<p id="notice" class="notice" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></p>
<div class="saved"><label for="saved">Saved reports</label><select id="saved"><option value="">Choose a report…</option></select><button id="open">Open report</button></div>
<section id="progress" class="panel" hidden><div class="progress-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">BUILDING YOUR REPORT</p><h2 id="phase"></h2><p id="progress-copy"></p></div><div><button id="resume" hidden>Resume</button><button id="stop">Stop</button></div></div><progress id="meter" max="18" value="0"></progress></section>
<section class="empty" id="empty"><span>01 / COMPARE</span><h2>One month or the bigger picture.</h2><p>Choose a client and a reporting period. Your report will show what changed, explain what each figure measures, and highlight questions to investigate.</p><div class="features"><article><h3>Search visibility</h3><p>Google clicks, impressions, click-through rate, average position and top queries.</p></article><article><h3>Website performance</h3><p>Users, traffic sources, landing pages, engagement and recorded key events.</p></article><article><h3>Ready for your client</h3><p>Add your own commentary, save the report, export figures or print to PDF.</p></article></div></section>
<article id="report" hidden><div class="report-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">NC DIGITAL · SEO & WEBSITE PERFORMANCE</p><h2 id="report-title"></h2><p id="dates"></p><p id="scope"></p></div><div class="report-actions"><button id="seo-email-open" class="primary" type="button">Email to client</button><button id="seo-share" type="button">Create client link</button><button id="export">Export figures</button><button id="print" class="primary">Print / save PDF</button></div></div>
<section id="seo-email-panel" class="panel sr-editor" hidden><p class="eyebrow">EMAIL THE REPORT</p><p class="muted">Sent from nathan@nc-digital.co.uk through the CRM with your usual sign-off. Replies land in your CRM inbox and a follow-up task is added for 3 days’ time.</p><form id="seo-email-form" class="sr-email-form"><div class="enq-row"><label>Contact name<input id="seo-email-name" maxlength="120"/></label><label>Email address<input id="seo-email-to" type="email" required maxlength="254"/></label></div><label>Message<textarea id="seo-email-message" rows="11" maxlength="8000"></textarea></label><div class="enq-actions"><button class="primary" type="submit" id="seo-email-send">Send email</button><button type="button" id="seo-email-close">Close</button><span id="seo-email-status" class="muted" role="status"></span></div></form><div id="seo-email-history"></div></section>
<section id="seo-share-panel" class="panel sr-editor" hidden><p class="eyebrow">CLIENT LINK</p><p class="muted">Send this link to the client. It shows the client report only. You get an email when they open it; your own previews from here don’t count.</p><div class="enq-row"><input id="seo-share-url" readonly aria-label="Client report link"/><div class="enq-actions"><button id="seo-share-copy" type="button">Copy link</button><a id="seo-share-open" class="button" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open ↗</a><button id="seo-share-off" type="button">Turn off link</button></div></div><p id="seo-share-stats" class="muted"></p></section>
<section class="panel sr-editor" id="enquiries-panel"><p class="eyebrow">WEBSITE FORM ENQUIRIES</p><h2>Add enquiries from the client’s website</h2><p class="muted">Export the form entries from their WordPress site as a CSV file (WPForms, Gravity Forms, Contact Form 7 / Flamingo, Fluent Forms and similar) and choose it here. Entries are counted by date in your browser; only the totals are saved, never names or messages. Phone taps and email clicks come from Google Analytics automatically.</p><div class="enq-row"><label class="enq-file">CSV export<input id="enq-file" type="file" accept=".csv,text/csv,text/plain"/></label><label>This period<input id="enq-current" type="number" min="0" step="1" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="e.g. 6"/></label><label>Previous period<input id="enq-previous" type="number" min="0" step="1" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="e.g. 2"/></label><div class="enq-actions"><button id="enq-save" class="primary" type="button">Save enquiries</button><button id="enq-clear" type="button">Remove</button></div></div><p id="enq-status" class="muted" role="status"></p></section>
<div id="client-doc"></div>
<details class="panel full-data" id="full-data"><summary>Full data and technical detail <span>(for you; not in the client report)</span></summary>
<div id="warnings"></div><section class="panel summary"><p class="eyebrow">PERIOD AT A GLANCE</p><div id="summary"></div></section>
<nav class="report-nav" aria-label="Report sections"><a href="#search-section">Google search</a><a href="#website-section">Website performance</a><a href="#acquisition-section">Acquisition</a><a href="#pages-section">Landing pages</a><a href="#actions-section">Actions & audience</a><a href="#notes-section">Client commentary</a></nav>
<section id="search-section" class="report-section"><div class="section-heading"><span>01</span><div><h2>Google search performance</h2><p>Search Console · Google Web Search · <span id="search-property"></span></p></div></div><div class="metric-grid" id="search-cards"></div><div id="search-tables"></div></section>
<section id="website-section" class="report-section"><div class="section-heading"><span>02</span><div><h2>Website performance</h2><p>GA4 web data. Traffic and actions recorded after tracking and consent apply.</p></div></div><div class="metric-grid" id="website-cards"></div><section class="panel trend"><h3>Daily website sessions</h3><p class="muted">Previous period in grey · current period in purple. Hover a point for the date and session count.</p><div id="trend"></div></section></section>
<section id="acquisition-section" class="report-section"><div class="section-heading"><span>03</span><div><h2>Where visitors came from</h2><p>Session acquisition. Organic Search includes search engines beyond Google.</p></div></div><div id="organic-cards" class="metric-grid"></div><div id="acquisition-tables"></div></section>
<section id="pages-section" class="report-section"><div class="section-heading"><span>04</span><div><h2>Landing pages</h2><p>The first page of the visit. Paths can represent multiple hostnames in a property.</p></div></div><div id="landing-table"></div></section>
<section id="actions-section" class="report-section"><div class="section-heading"><span>05</span><div><h2>Actions & audience</h2><p>Key events reflect your GA4 configuration. An event count is not a count of verified leads.</p></div></div><div id="audience-tables"></div></section>
</details>
<section id="notes-section" class="report-section panel"><p class="eyebrow">WORK THIS PERIOD</p><h2>SEO pages created &amp; optimised</h2><p class="muted">One page per line. Start a group with a line ending in a colon, e.g. “New Service Pages – Newport:”. Totals are counted for you. This appears in the client report under “SEO Pages Created &amp; Optimised”.</p><label class="notes-label" for="work">Pages created and optimised<textarea id="work" maxlength="8000" rows="10" placeholder="New Pillar Pages:&#10;Renewable Energy Installers Newport&#10;&#10;New Service Pages – Newport:&#10;Solar Panel Installation&#10;Battery Storage"></textarea></label><div class="notes-actions"><button id="work-suggest" type="button">Add new pages found in Search Console</button></div><label class="notes-label" for="notes">Notes &amp; next steps <span class="hint">optional · shown at the end of the report</span><textarea id="notes" maxlength="6000" rows="7" placeholder="Work completed this period…&#10;&#10;Context behind the results…&#10;&#10;Priorities for the next period…"></textarea></label><div class="notes-actions"><button id="save-notes">Save work &amp; notes</button><span id="notes-status" role="status"></span></div><p id="print-notes"></p></section>
<footer class="methodology"><h3>How to read this report</h3><p>These are measured changes, not proof that a particular SEO change caused them. Seasonality, campaigns, tracking and consent can affect the figures. Completed calendar periods can contain different numbers of days; daily averages are provided for volume metrics where useful.</p><p>Google Analytics dates use the selected property’s time zone. Search Console uses Pacific dates and finalised search data. GA4 sessions and Search Console clicks measure different things and should not be expected to match. Missing rows and zero baselines are labelled explicitly.</p><p>Tables show a shortlist, not every row. Site totals are requested separately and are not calculated by adding table rows. A person can appear in multiple segments. Historical key events depend on the configuration in place at the time. Recent data can still change.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://developers.google.com/analytics/devguides/reporting/data/v1/api-schema" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics metric definitions</a> · <a href="https://developers.google.com/webmaster-tools/v1/searchanalytics/query" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Search Console reporting</a></p><p id="generated"></p></footer>
</article></main><script>import '../../scripts/analytics-reports.js';</script></body></html>
